\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Sweet is the memory of Thy grace,
\par My God, my heavenly King:
\par Let age to age Thy righteousness
\par In sounds of glory sing.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. God reigns on high, but not confines
\par His bounty to the skies;
\par Through the whole earth His goodness shines,
\par And every  want supplies.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. With longing eyes the creatures wait
\par On Thee for daily food;
\par Thy liberal hand provides them meat,
\par And fills their mouths with good.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. How kind are Thy compassions, Lord,
\par How slow Thine anger moves;
\par But soon He sends His pardoning word,
\par To cheer the souls  He loves.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Creatures, with all their endless race,
\par Thy power and praise proclaim;
\par But we, who taste Thy richer grace,
\par Delight to bless Thy name.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

